What is an Agricultural Harvesting Robot?
Agricultural Harvesting Robots are purpose built platforms that combine AI driven perception, multi spectral imaging, and dexterous end effectors to execute the complex task of fruit and vegetable picking. Unlike conventional mechanized harvesters that rely on bulk cutting or shaking, these robots make crop by crop decisions in real time, assessing ripeness, size and surface integrity before executing a gentle grasp. The technology stack typically includes high resolution RGB NIR cameras, lidar based navigation, real time edge computing, and adaptive gripper designs that can be re configured for different crop geometries.
